        'DECIDE the peer-selling guardrail before forum member-posting (Phase 2): community & discovery only vs classifieds — affects FCA/scam-dispute exposure',
        'ACCOUNTS & MESSAGING OVERHAUL (decided 20 Aug, plan in refs). Phases A, B, C DONE and D nearly done (messaging, channel chooser, buyer push and the seller console threads are live; remaining in D: postcode delivery prefill, then Phase F: the admin channel-preference card off contact_events)',
        'Journey test is scheduled locally 4x/day — move it to a Railway cron (node journey-test.js --quiet) so it runs when the PC is off and picks up the Twilio vars that are already set there. Local .env needs ALERT_TWILIO_* for the SMS to fire from here.',
        'Buyer postcode at sign-up is specifically to prefill one-click SMR delivery quotes — wire it into the delivery enquiry rather than asking for a full address again',
        'SECURITY: the seller setup link is replayable (sellers.password_set has no column, so the one-time guard never fires) and SELLER_SETUP_KEY is one shared key sitting in the welcome email of every approved seller — anyone holding it can set the password on any approved seller who has not set one. Retired by the single email-code login in Phase B; until then it is an account-takeover route',
